  "issue_title": "[bug] rsvd.basis: concatenate/QR peak doubles (n,m) after sketches \u2014 unbudgeted VRAM spike",
  "issue_body": "\ufeff## Summary\n\n`rsvd.basis` correctly charges prior sketch parts while *streaming*, but then keeps all three `(n, w_i)` parts live and does `xp.concatenate(parts)` into another `(n, m)` buffer before QR. Peak is roughly **2\u00d7(n\u00b7m)** for assembly alone (parts + Y), then QR adds another `(n, m)` \u2014 a spike that is never charged against `--vram-fraction`.\n\nOn MPS (static `free_compute_bytes`), sketches can succeed and then OOM at concatenate/QR.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nPreallocate the `(n, m)` assembly buffer, charge it as `extra_fixed_bytes` on every sketch, copy each sketch into a column slice and drop it immediately \u2014 no `concatenate` of all parts.\n\nDistinct from #265 (prior-parts stream charge) and #210 (frac threading).\n\nOpen zone: `strategy/` only.\r\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-17T21:27:18.000Z",
